1. (CLL, Chapter 3): "Lojban is designed so that any properly spoken Lojban=
=20
utterance can be uniquely transcribed in writing, and any properly written=
=20
Lojban can be spoken so as to be uniquely reproduced by another person. As=
=20
a consequence, the standard Lojban orthography must assign to each distinct=
=20
sound, or phoneme, a unique letter or symbol."=20

My reading of this is that there is only one way to pronounce u, which is=
=20
(among others) the plain Spanish "u".=20

2. It may be that speakers of other languages can pronounce it as "w" (and=
=20
I can forgive them), but I can/do clearly pronounce it as plain "u": .ui =
=3D=20
"u" + "i"

Anyway, this is just my humble opinion.

mu'o mi'e la .albaros


